UberSDR: restore the "always open" FM squelch idiom

WHAT
  Treat a squelch-open threshold at or below 1e-30 -- the -999 dB our presets
  use -- as "no squelch", in fm.c and wfm.c.

WHY CONFIG CANNOT DO THIS
  ka9q-radio used to map squelch-open <= -999 to exactly 0.0 (modes.c) and skip
  the squelch when both thresholds were zero (fm.c).  Both halves were removed,
  so -999 is now just dB2power(-999) = 1.26e-100: tiny, but positive.
  That is not equivalent, because chan->fm.snr can be zero or negative -- the
  cheap estimator is bb_power/noise - 1 and is used unclamped, and the variance
  estimator is clamped with max(0.0, snr).  Since dB2power() cannot return
  anything but a positive number, NO threshold keeps the gate open on a
  noise-only channel.  radiod then emits no RTP at all for that channel, which
  UberSDR sees as FM having a squelch nobody asked for.

WHY UBERSDR CANNOT DO THIS
  The decision is radiod's; by the time UberSDR could act there is no stream.
  UberSDR gates audio itself (set_audio_gate / min_snr) and needs radiod to pass
  everything through.

WHAT WOULD LET US DROP IT
  Upstream reinstating an explicit way to disable the FM squelch -- the old
  sentinel, or a "squelch = no" key.  Worth raising upstream: -999 dB is a
  documented idiom that now silently means something else.

Applies to ka9q-radio cce087e2090ed71889697f3831f34ef7825d9a44.
Verified: fm.o and wfm.o compile warning-free.

diff --git a/src/fm.c b/src/fm.c
index 59c071d..c90eda8 100644
--- a/src/fm.c
+++ b/src/fm.c
@@ -40,6 +40,17 @@ int demod_fm(void *arg){
   if(!isfinite(chan->squelch.close) || chan->squelch.close == 0)
     chan->squelch.close = 4; // close below ~ +6 dB
 
+  /* UberSDR: restore the "always open" squelch idiom.
+     A squelch-open threshold below this is nobody's literal intent; it is the
+     conventional way of asking for no squelch at all, and our presets say -999 dB.
+     It has to be a special case rather than just a very low threshold, because
+     chan->fm.snr is zero or negative on a noise-only channel -- the estimate is
+     bb_power/noise - 1, taken unclamped in the cheap path -- while dB2power()
+     can never return anything but a positive number.  So no threshold, however
+     small, keeps the gate open, and the channel emits no RTP at all.
+     UberSDR gates audio itself via set_audio_gate/min_snr and needs radiod to
+     pass everything through. */
+
   chan->fm.devmax = 5000.; // nominal peak deviation Hz
   chan->fm.modbw = 3000.;   // maximum modulating frequency Hz
 
@@ -147,7 +158,7 @@ int demod_fm(void *arg){
        If at any time the SNR >= open threshold, the sequence is aborted, the timer is restarted and normal operation continues
     */
     int const squelch_state_max = chan->squelch.tail + 5;
-    if(chan->fm.snr >= chan->squelch.open){
+    if(chan->squelch.open <= SQUELCH_ALWAYS_OPEN || chan->fm.snr >= chan->squelch.open){
       squelch_state = squelch_state_max; // hold open
     } else if(squelch_state > 0 && (chan->fm.snr < chan->squelch.close || squelch_state < squelch_state_max)){
       squelch_state--; // initiate or continue closing
diff --git a/src/radio.h b/src/radio.h
index fd2e6a9..5ddc115 100644
--- a/src/radio.h
+++ b/src/radio.h
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@
 
 
 
+/* UberSDR: threshold below which a squelch-open setting means "no squelch at all".
+   See the comment in fm.c; presets express this as squelch-open = -999 (dB). */
+#define SQUELCH_ALWAYS_OPEN (1e-30)
+
 /**
